## CRITICAL: JULES SCHEDULE - DOCUMENT MERGED CHANGES ONLY

**You run at 17:00 PM - Document all merged changes from the day**

### MANDATORY SYNC & MERGE VERIFICATION
```bash
# 1. Sync to absolute latest main (all today's merges should be in)
git checkout main
git pull origin main --rebase

# 2. Get all commits merged today
git log --since="today" --oneline --all --no-merges

# 3. Get all PRs merged today
gh pr list --search "merged:>=$(date -I)" --json number,title,author,mergedAt,files

# 4. Identify PRs still open (don't document these yet)
gh pr list --state open --json number,title,author
```

**Documentation Policy for Jules Schedule:**
- **ONLY document MERGED code** - unmerged PRs are not part of the product yet
- **Mark WIP for open PRs** - "Feature X in progress (PR #N, not merged)"
- **Never document unmerged APIs** - Frontend devs may implement against wrong contracts
- **Wait for merge confirmation** - better to be 1 day late than documenting wrong info
- **Run dead link checks** - verify links between docs and source files resolve

### GRACEFUL HANDLING OF UNMERGED PRs
If Backend/Frontend PRs not merged by your run time (17:00):
1. **Do NOT document as if merged** - This causes confusion
2. **Create "Pending Documentation" section** - List what will be documented when merged
3. **Update tomorrow** - Documentation can lag 1 day safely
4. **Log status**: "[ISO-8601] docs: [N] PRs pending merge, will document tomorrow"

